<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>HelioForge Energy Lab | Hybrid Energy Research &amp; Learning</title><meta name="description" content="Explore hybrid-energy architectures, learning activities and bundled scenario results in HelioForge’s free browser research preview."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta name="google-site-verification" content="wZk3bMiBHxDWxN4EmERLH9sBza2QlvsTaxbOSBncrvw"><meta name="author" content="Mohammad Rezwan Khan"><meta name="theme-color" content="#132923"><link rel="canonical" href="https://mkgrid.co.technology/"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/domain.css"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:site_name" content="HelioForge"><meta property="og:title" content="HelioForge Energy Lab | Hybrid Energy Research &amp; Learning"><meta property="og:description" content="Explore hybrid-energy architectures, learning activities and bundled scenario results in HelioForge’s free browser research preview."><meta property="og:url" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/"><meta property="og:image" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/social-preview.png"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="HelioForge hybrid-energy research preview"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="HelioForge Energy Lab | Hybrid Energy Research &amp; Learning"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Explore hybrid-energy architectures, learning activities and bundled scenario results in HelioForge’s free browser research preview."><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/social-preview.png"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#website","name":"HelioForge","url":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/","publisher":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]},"inLanguage":"en"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#page","name":"HelioForge Energy Lab | Hybrid Energy Research & Learning","url":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/","description":"Explore hybrid-energy architectures, learning activities and bundled scenario results in HelioForge’s free browser research preview.","inLanguage":"en","dateModified":"2026-10-26","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#website"},"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]}},{"@type":"SoftwareApplication","@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#app","name":"HelioForge","url":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/","description":"Explore hybrid-energy architectures, learning activities and bundled scenario results in HelioForge’s free browser research preview.","applicationCategory":"EducationalApplication","operatingSystem":"Web browser","isAccessibleForFree":true,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]},"featureList":["Browse hybrid-energy architectures and inspect their labeled system layouts.","Read architecture-linked lessons with experiment steps and self-check questions.","Review bundled scenario examples and compare visible energy assumptions and outcomes.","Explore 59 distinct experimental studies across twelve views, with Python-generated examples and explicit model boundaries.","Inspect timelines, sensitivity maps, tariff inputs, signed local evidence and complete result exports.","Calculate browser energy balances, sweeps, local sensitivity and A/B deltas; export verified SHA-256 manifests."],"softwareHelp":{"@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/methodology/#page"},"sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab"]}]}</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/engineering-hero/v1/integration/vanilla/host.css"><script type="module" src="/assets/engineering-hero/v1/integration/vanilla/khan-grid-hero.js"></script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="/">H<span>↗</span> HelioForge</a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="/run/">Open app</a><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a><a href="/about/">About</a></nav></header><main id="main"><section class="app-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">HYBRID ENERGY / RESEARCH / LEARNING</p><h1>Explore the system.<br>Understand its limits.</h1><p class="lead">Explore hybrid-system designs and inspect assumptions. The Terminal workbench calculates new bounded 24-hour synthetic energy-balance cases in your browser; advanced models require the local Python application.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/run/">Open HelioForge preview ↗</a><a href="/methodology/">Read the model boundaries</a></div><p class="micro">Free browser preview · No sign-in · Bundled example results</p></div><figure class="app-preview"><img src="/preview.png" alt="HelioForge’s actual hybrid-energy learning interface" width="1440" height="1000" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Actual interface. Terminal cases calculate in-browser; advanced models require the local Python app.</figcaption></figure></section><section class="engineering-hero" aria-labelledby="engineering-hero-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING / FIELD NOTES</p><h2 id="engineering-hero-heading">See the system behind the study</h2><p class="lead">A short visual introduction to the engineering context sits alongside this overview. The hosted preview remains synthetic and the film does not validate a design or model.</p></div><khan-grid-hero site="mkgrid" mode="video" video-src="/assets/engineering-hero/v1/hero-1080p60.mp4" poster-src="/assets/engineering-hero/v1/poster.png" hide-cta><img slot="poster" src="/assets/engineering-hero/v1/poster.png" alt="Poster for the engineering film introducing system context" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></khan-grid-hero></section><section class="content-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">EXPLORE</p><h2>Follow the energy and the assumptions</h2><ul class="feature-list"><li>Browse hybrid-energy architectures and inspect their labeled system layouts.</li><li>Read architecture-linked lessons with experiment steps and self-check questions.</li><li>Review bundled scenario examples and compare visible energy assumptions and outcomes.</li><li>Explore 59 distinct experimental studies across twelve views, with Python-generated examples and explicit model boundaries.</li><li>Inspect timelines, sensitivity maps, tariff inputs, signed local evidence and complete result exports.</li><li>Calculate browser energy balances, sweeps, local sensitivity and A/B deltas; export verified SHA-256 manifests.</li></ul></div><div id="how-to-use"><p class="eyebrow">START HERE</p><h2>Try it in three steps</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Choose an architecture and inspect its components and stated assumptions.</li><li>Open a linked lesson and follow its experiment prompts and self-check.</li><li>Review a bundled scenario result and compare its energy and cost measures.</li></ol></div></section><section class="boundary"><div><p class="eyebrow">CAPABILITY &amp; LIMITS</p><h2>A research preview with a visible boundary</h2></div><div><p>The catalogue contains <strong>36 architectures</strong> and <strong>36 linked lessons</strong>. In the separate local Python application, 19 architectures have electricity-balance screens and 17 remain study-only. This hosted preview shows bundled examples and a separate browser Terminal energy-balance model; it does not perform new Python calculations.</p><ul><li>The standalone browser preview uses bundled examples and does not run new Python calculations or optimization.</li><li>Advanced numerical studies and optimization require the local Python API. The browser Terminal model is a direct hourly energy balance, not an optimizer.</li><li>Models are educational research screens, not calibrated plant controls, forecasts, or investment advice.</li></ul><p><a href="/methodology/">Read what is implemented and what remains a study →</a></p></div></section><section class="faq"><p class="eyebrow">COMMON QUESTIONS</p><h2>Before you explore</h2><details><summary>Can the standalone preview calculate a new scenario?</summary><p>Yes, the Terminal workbench calculates bounded 24-hour energy-balance cases in the browser. Advanced studies require the separate local Python app.</p></details><details><summary>Are the model results operational guidance?</summary><p>No. They are bounded research and learning examples with explicit assumptions, not a plant controller or calibrated digital twin.</p></details><details><summary>Does this website call external AI?</summary><p>No. The public browser preview has no external AI integration. The separate local application’s optional provider adapter requires explicit configuration and consent.</p></details><details><summary>Does local progress transfer from MKLab?</summary><p>No. Browser storage belongs to the current origin and device. Local progress saved on another domain is not automatically transferred.</p></details></section><section class="release"><h2>Source, methods and evidence</h2><p>Maintained by <a href="https://mrkhan.co.technology/">Mohammad Rezwan Khan</a>. Updated <time datetime="2026-10-26">2026-10-26</time>.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab">Public source and verification</a> · <a href="/app.json">App facts</a> · <a href="/llms.txt">Plain-text guide</a> · <a href="/NOTICES.txt">Notices</a></p><p class="micro">Source revision 74d6730e3832 · Browser runtime SHA-256 a12384067a75ab7a</p></section></main><footer><a class="wordmark" href="/">HelioForge</a><p>Explore energy systems. Inspect their assumptions.</p><a href="https://mklab.co.technology/">Explore MKLab apps →</a></footer></body></html>